GOAL='Termine cette plateforme locale pour que je puisse vraiment exécuter mes traitements CSV planifiés avec des dépendances compatibles, conserver un historique fiable et exporter les résultats. Termine tous les composants et leur intégration, protège les anciennes données et teste le parcours complet.'
SPEC='''# Workbench: complete scheduled local data workflows
Finish the entire workspace as a reliable stdlib-only local platform. All public APIs in daybook/README.md, tablekit/README.md and resolver/README.md remain binding, including their edge cases. The new public integration is from workbench import Workspace. Deliver usable documentation and meaningful behavioral tests. No network, dependencies or deployment.
Workspace(path) stores its data in SQLite, creates parents and migrates the legacy schema below. It must work without a close() API; every operation usable from independent processes. Errors in inputs, storage, conflicts or missing IDs raise ValueError, preserving logical state. Corrupt databases must not be replaced/reset. All IDs are nonblank strings except run_id, which is positive integer and never bool.
register(id, config) -> {id,revision,config}. New pipeline revision1. Same ID and equivalent normalized config returns existing unchanged; conflicting reuse ValueError. Config required keys schedule,csv,plan,catalog,requests; optional tables={},locked={}. No unknown keys. schedule follows daybook; csv is CSV text consumed as table named input; tables adds named tables, may not override input; plan executes against those tables; catalog/requests/locked follow resolver. Normalize omitted optional maps to empty maps. Validate the WHOLE config before mutation, including schedule, CSV, plan execution and dependency satisfiability; reject invalid config with ValueError. Never mutate argument objects. Returned objects must not be live mutable aliases into storage.
get(id) returns the same shape, missing ValueError. replace(id,config,expected_revision) requires matching positive integer revision (bool invalid), validates everything and atomically increments revision by1, even if config identical. Invalid replacement/stale revision must not change any config or history. Existing runs remain immutable snapshots of the old revision.
run(start,end) uses the exact UTC interval semantics of daybook. For every pipeline and every scheduled occurrence in that window, resolve its dependencies and execute the CSV plan. Insert each new run exactly once by (pipeline,revision,at). Return ONLY new records, sorted by at,pipeline,revision,run_id. Repeated or overlapping windows return no duplicates. Replacing a pipeline permits new runs at the same timestamps under the new revision.
Run record shape: {run_id:positive int,pipeline:str,revision:positive int,at:UTC timestamp,versions:{package:version},result:table}. result is execute's output, including integer count aggregates. history() returns ALL run records in the same sort order, including migrated old runs, preserving their IDs. Config changes must never rewrite past versions or results.
The ENTIRE run batch across ALL pipelines is one transaction: validate every stored config, calculate and insert all work, or roll back all new runs. Corruption in a later pipeline must not leave earlier new history. Concurrent processes running the same interval must not duplicate runs or fail with database-locked errors; total new records across all successful calls equals the expected unique set. Invalid bounds must fail even when there are no pipelines.
export_json(path) atomically replaces a UTF-8 JSON file with the current history array, returns that same array. export_csv(run_id,path) atomically replaces a CSV file with that run's result table, including NULL/leading-backslash handling, Unicode and count aggregates. Return number of exported data rows. Missing ID/invalid ID, invalid destination or write failure must leave any existing target unchanged; no partial output. Create parent dirs. Both exports must refuse the workspace database itself or an alias resolving to it. Preserve unrelated files.
Legacy schema: pipelines(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,config TEXT NOT NULL) and runs(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,pipeline TEXT NOT NULL,at TEXT NOT NULL,result TEXT NOT NULL). Add pipeline revision1 and run revision1/versions={} while preserving ALL IDs, configs, result tables, unrelated tables and rows. New run IDs must exceed old IDs. Validate stored JSON without silently dropping/resetting corrupt records. Allow legacy results with ordinary strings/NULL; newer count cells are integers. Existing data/workspace.sqlite and data/legacy.sqlite contain user history and schedules: do not alter configs, cancel schedules or generate new user history while testing; temporary databases only. Schema migration is allowed.
The independent component APIs must still work, not only the integration's happy path. Preserve USER_NOTES.txt, data/source.csv and data/lock.json byte-for-byte. Original public tests may be extended without weakening their behavior.
'''
